{
  "description": "MindRoom tool positions (io.mindroom.tool_trace version 3). 'sent' is a reply as the backend renders it, its markers in the text (version 2); 'wire' is what it sends to Matrix: the text without the markers of its calls, and on each call 'body_line', the number of lines of the wire body before its marker, and 'at', the number of top-level blocks of the wire formatted_body before it (null: the call has no such key). A top-level block is a top-level element with its content, a top-level void element, or a run of top-level text with a non-whitespace character. A reader puts each marker back as 'sent' has it: a body line before line 'body_line' with a blank line after it, or at the end after a blank line; a <p> before block 'at' or at the end. A call without the key gets no marker, and one whose position is no integer, is past the end or lies before an earlier call's goes at the end. 'wire' null: the text would not read back exactly, so the backend sends 'sent' as it is. Shared by mindroom (tests/fixtures) and mindroom-chat (src/app/matrix/protocol/__fixtures__); change both copies together.",
